      "text": [
        " قَالَ عَلِيٌّ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ : \"يَدُ اَللَّهِ فَوْقَ رَأْسِ اَلْحَاكِمِ تُرَفْرِفُ بِالرَّحْمَةِ، فَإِذَا حَافَ فِي اَلْحُكْمِ وَكَلَهُ اَللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ إِلَى نَفْسِهِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3228 - Al-Sakuni narrated with his chain of transmission that Commander of the Faithful Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib (as) said:\n\"The hand of Allah (swt) hovers with mercy above the head of the judge. But if he deviates in judgment, Allah (swt), the Mighty and Majestic, leaves him to himself.\""
        ]
      }
